== governing case P1G canonical: M_cb(<300 kpc) 4.91e+13 Msun, mean Sigma_cb >= 3.629e-02 g/cm^2, rho_cb 2.94e-26 g/cm^3
(a) mean excess N_H if spread: 1.63e+22 cm^-2 against 2e+20 (PROVISIONAL, Chandra/XMM N_H agreeing with Galactic HI at about that level, from memory): diffuse EXCLUDED, must be clumped
    clumped and grey (N_c >= 1e22) with covering f_c <= 0.10 needs Sigma_c >= 3.629e-01 g/cm^2 (N_c >= 1.63e+23)
(b) Bullet main gas central rho 1.79e-26 g/cm^3 (n_e 9.2e-03), UX6 model; swept column over 1 Mpc 5.530e-02; need Sigma_c >= 3x = 1.659e-01; self-gravity G Sigma^2 >= rho v^2 at 4700 km/s needs Sigma_c >= 2.436e-01
(c) saturated heat flux 5.15e-02 erg/cm^2/s at T 1e8 K, n_e 3e-3 (Cowie and McKee 1977 form); mass evaporated over 1/H0: 6.597e-01 g/cm^2 (x 1/100 magnetic suppression: 6.6e-03, reported only)
    cloud-cloud collisions, t_coll = Sigma_c/(rho_cb sigma_v) >= 1/H0 at sigma_v 1000 km/s: Sigma_c >= 1.296e+00 g/cm^2 (sigma/m <= 0.77 cm^2/g)
(d) a cloud is a microlens when Sigma_c > Sigma_cr = c^2/(4 pi G D), D 1 Gpc: 0.347 g/cm^2. CBDM share of the model mass at 300 kpc: 0.50 (gate 0.10, PROVISIONAL reading of Oguri+2018)

== cloud window: survival needs Sigma_c >= 1.296 g/cm^2 (max of a, b, c); not a microlens needs Sigma_c < 0.347. Window CLOSED: ratio 3.73
   with conduction suppressed 100x: need >= 1.296; window CLOSED, ratio 3.73
   P1 canonical: need >= 1.388, ratio 4.00
   P2 canonical: need >= 1.876, ratio 5.40
   P3 canonical: need >= 1.462, ratio 4.21
   a cloud at the window's lower edge, T 2.73 K: bound mass c_s^4/(G^2 Sigma) 8.1e-04 Msun, radius 42 AU, free-fall 1.7e+03 yr; heavier clouds collapse unless supported, and would make stars or brown dwarfs

== object classes (gates a-e)
  dense cold H2 clouds (sub-critical) a fail   b fail   c fail   d pass       e pass      -> does not survive; window closed at ratio 3.73 (need/limit); collisions alone need 1.30 against Sigma_cr 0.35
  dense cold H2 clouds (super-critical) a pass   b pass   c pass   d fail       e pass      -> does not survive; compact enough to microlens; caustic-crossing limit 1e-5-1e2 Msun (Oguri+2018, PROVISIONAL)
  sub-Earth H/He bodies (< 1e-5 Msun) a pass   b pass   c untested d pass       e pass      -> does not survive; below caustic-crossing range; survival of H/He solids not computed here (PROVISIONAL: thought to sublimate), NOT ESTABLISHED
  Jupiters, brown dwarfs (1e-3-0.08) a pass   b pass   c pass   d fail       e pass      -> does not survive; inside the caustic-crossing mass range at a high share of the core mass
  stellar remnants (WD, NS, stellar BH) a pass   b pass   c pass   d fail       e pass      -> does not survive; microlensing range, and progenitors' metals: ~2 % yield on 4.8x the gas gives ~0.1 of the gas mass in metals against the ICM's ~0.004 (0.3 solar), ~25x over (PROVISIONAL)
  massive BHs: heating of cluster galaxies over 1/H0 reaches sigma^2 at M_BH 1.4e+09 Msun (sigma 200 km/s), 8.7e+07 (50 km/s); total Bondi-Hoyle L at efficiency 0.1: 1e+02 Msun 3.0e+38 erg/s, 1e+04 Msun 3.0e+40 erg/s, 1e+06 Msun 3.0e+42 erg/s
  massive black holes (1e2 to ~1e7 Msun) a pass   b pass   c pass   d pass       e pass      -> SURVIVES; above the caustic range, below galaxy heating; accretion luminosity 3e+42 erg/s at 1e6 against a core L_X ~1e44-1e45; no known channel makes ~5x the gas in BHs without stars or metals; millilensing not computed

(e) BBN with D/H: Omega_b h^2 0.02166 (Cooke+2018, PROVISIONAL, from memory; not Planck) -> rho_b 4.07e-31 g/cm^3, h-free
